WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.353
Second Normal Form becomes especially relevant when
a table has a composite

00:00:04.379 --> 00:00:10.070
key Suppose the row is identified by appointment ID
and service code

00:00:10.096 --> 00:00:16.046
together Now ask whether every non-key column
depends on that whole combination

00:00:17.803 --> 00:00:23.121
Appointment start time depends only on the
appointment Service name and standard

00:00:23.147 --> 00:00:27.858
price depend only on the service code Quantity and
the captured charge

00:00:27.884 --> 00:00:33.293
may depend on the combination of appointment and
service The columns that

00:00:33.306 --> 00:00:36.174
depend on only part of the composite key should be
moved to

00:00:36.201 --> 00:00:42.033
the table where that dependency belongs This leads
toward separate appointment

00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:47.794
service and appointment-service tables The goal is
to align each fact

00:00:47.807 --> 00:00:49.820
with the key that actually determines it
